{
  "set": "public-record-eval-2",
  "sealed": "2026-11-25, before any DS-N1 run on these texts",
  "source": "Study 014 (branch claude/engine-eval-v8-2026-10-01): 30 public EEOC federal-sector appellate decisions (BACKGROUND sections, published in the repository) and the AI drafts made from them on 2026-10-02.",
  "truth": "Study 014 measured, with a deterministic extractor and a reconstruction test fixed before its run, that P1 concise summaries lost most record citations and quotations (reconstruction 77.3% vs 96.7% from the source) while P4 JRS-guided drafts kept them (97.3%). P1 is therefore the lossy condition and P4 the retaining condition.",
  "run_settings": "record = draft text; source = the public decision text; record_class workplace_investigation_report; data_classification public_record_test.",
  "signal": "open findings after review plus omission questions (findOmissions).",
  "rule_primary": "For each of the 60 source-drafter pairs, the P1 draft should receive a higher signal than the P4 draft. Success: P1 higher in a majority of non-tied pairs, two-sided sign test p < 0.05.",
  "rule_secondary": "READY_FOR_HUMAN_FINALIZATION rate for P4 drafts should exceed that for P1 drafts.",
  "risk_stated_in_advance": "P1 drafts are shorter, so they contain fewer sentences that can be flagged; the tool may give them fewer findings. If so the primary rule fails and that is reported.",
